From: uwe@kleine-koenig.org (=?UTF-8?q?Uwe=20Kleine-K=C3=B6nig?=)
Date: Fri,  8 Jul 2016 23:22:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx6qdl: don't configure reserved pad settings
Message-ID: <1468012974-27180-1-git-send-email-uwe@kleine-koenig.org>
To: linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
List-Id: linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org

Several dts files set a bit in the SPEED field for pads
RGMII_{R,T}{XC,D0,D1,D2,D3,X_CTL}, but that doesn't exist. Writing there
doesn't have an effect and the bit reads as zero.

Signed-off-by: Uwe Kleine-K?nig <uwe@kleine-koenig.org>
---
Hello,

As many boards have the same bug here, I guess that's the result of
largely doing copy&paste to setup the MDIO bus.

Best regards
Uwe

